{
  "source": "Prompts/does-ai-think-6.mp4",
  "duration": 204.7535625,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 5.82,
      "text": "You type a question into a text box, hit enter, and watch as a cursor blinks to life,"
    },
    {
      "start": 6.34,
      "end": 9.48,
      "text": "generating a response that feels entirely natural."
    },
    {
      "start": 10.26,
      "end": 13.96,
      "text": "It can break down a complex poem, land a halfway decent joke,"
    },
    {
      "start": 14.46,
      "end": 17.68,
      "text": "and even apologize if you point out a mistake in its logic."
    },
    {
      "start": 18.46,
      "end": 22.52,
      "text": "After a few back and forths, it creates a powerful psychological effect."
    },
    {
      "start": 23.1,
      "end": 28.48,
      "text": "It is hard to shake the feeling that there is actually a conscious mind sitting on the other side of the screen."
    },
    {
      "start": 29.1,
      "end": 33.5,
      "text": "But when artificial intelligence behaves this way, is it actually thinking?"
    },
    {
      "start": 34.2,
      "end": 39.02,
      "text": "When it strings together coherent sentences, is it understanding the world the same way you do?"
    },
    {
      "start": 39.66,
      "end": 44.16,
      "text": "But sounding like a person doesn't tell you whether it understands things the way a person does."
    },
    {
      "start": 44.82,
      "end": 47.06,
      "text": "To see how an illusion of fluency works,"
    },
    {
      "start": 47.46,
      "end": 51.6,
      "text": "philosophers often point to a famous thought experiment called the Chinese Room."
    },
    {
      "start": 52.3,
      "end": 54.44,
      "text": "Imagine a person locked inside a room."
    },
    {
      "start": 54.88,
      "end": 57.4,
      "text": "They do not speak or read a single word of Chinese."
    },
    {
      "start": 58.12,
      "end": 62.8,
      "text": "The only thing they have in this room is a massive, rigidly structured rule book."
    },
    {
      "start": 63.42,
      "end": 64.08,
      "text": "Here is the setup."
    },
    {
      "start": 64.8,
      "end": 68.6,
      "text": "People standing outside the room slide a note written in Chinese under the door."
    },
    {
      "start": 69.06,
      "end": 70.22,
      "text": "It asks, how are you?"
    },
    {
      "start": 70.68,
      "end": 72.94,
      "text": "The person inside cannot read a bit of it."
    },
    {
      "start": 73.32,
      "end": 78.74,
      "text": "Instead, they simply take those unfamiliar shapes and visually match them on a giant look-up chart."
    },
    {
      "start": 79.38,
      "end": 81.16,
      "text": "They blindly follow the rule book's instructions,"
    },
    {
      "start": 81.7,
      "end": 85.68,
      "text": "select the exact matching set of symbols for the reply, and slide it back out."
    },
    {
      "start": 85.68,
      "end": 88.96,
      "text": "To anyone outside, it looks like fluent Chinese conversation."
    },
    {
      "start": 90.08,
      "end": 92.44,
      "text": "But the person inside comprehends nothing."
    },
    {
      "start": 93.48,
      "end": 95.56,
      "text": "A convincing answer doesn't prove understanding."
    },
    {
      "start": 96.82,
      "end": 98.66,
      "text": "The Chinese Room illustrates a distinction."
    },
    {
      "start": 99.58,
      "end": 103.6,
      "text": "Producing an answer and understanding it aren't necessarily the same thing."
    },
    {
      "start": 104.42,
      "end": 108.52,
      "text": "Now, mapping this onto modern, large language models requires a slate adjustment."
    },
    {
      "start": 109.38,
      "end": 112.36,
      "text": "The machine does not consult a physical paper rule book."
    },
    {
      "start": 112.82,
      "end": 115.62,
      "text": "An LLM doesn't follow a literal rule book."
    },
    {
      "start": 116.28,
      "end": 119.42,
      "text": "It uses patterns learned during training to predict its response."
    },
    {
      "start": 120.22,
      "end": 124.04,
      "text": "It calculates the mathematically optimal sequence of text based on its data."
    },
    {
      "start": 124.92,
      "end": 129.76,
      "text": "A perfectly fluent conversation is simply an invalid metric for judging true comprehension."
    },
    {
      "start": 130.7,
      "end": 134.72,
      "text": "Look at this comparison chart mapping human thought directly against machine processes."
    },
    {
      "start": 135.58,
      "end": 138.6,
      "text": "The mechanical gap becomes clear when you view them side by side."
    },
    {
      "start": 139.16,
      "end": 142.96,
      "text": "Regarding experience and meaning, you draw on things you have lived through."
    },
    {
      "start": 143.68,
      "end": 145.76,
      "text": "You connect words to what they mean in your life."
    },
    {
      "start": 146.46,
      "end": 150.08,
      "text": "AI solely uses learned patterns in what you tell it in a prompt."
    },
    {
      "start": 150.86,
      "end": 155.16,
      "text": "For word choice, you actively select words to express what you want to say."
    },
    {
      "start": 155.98,
      "end": 159.2,
      "text": "AI algorithmically predicts the next word, then repeats."
    },
    {
      "start": 160.06,
      "end": 163.44,
      "text": "And when it comes to uncertainty, you can notice when you are unsure."
    },
    {
      "start": 164.4,
      "end": 166.64,
      "text": "AI can sound certain even when it is wrong."
    },
    {
      "start": 167.18,
      "end": 169.78,
      "text": "The final text block might read perfectly to us,"
    },
    {
      "start": 170.2,
      "end": 173.36,
      "text": "but similar looking answers can come from very different processes."
    },
    {
      "start": 174.34,
      "end": 179.76,
      "text": "Acknowledging this lack of understanding does not mean artificial intelligence is useless or dumb."
    },
    {
      "start": 180.42,
      "end": 184.26,
      "text": "These models can accomplish incredibly impressive, complex work."
    },
    {
      "start": 185.08,
      "end": 188.8,
      "text": "But utility and cognition are two different targets."
    },
    {
      "start": 189.82,
      "end": 194.88,
      "text": "Generating a human sounding output is never enough to prove that a machine grasps the material."
    },
    {
      "start": 195.52,
      "end": 197.58,
      "text": "Sounds human works differently."
    },
    {
      "start": 198.52,
      "end": 200.92,
      "text": "A convincing answer doesn't prove understanding."
    }
  ],
